{"title":"Career Roadmap · Environmental Surveyor","role":"Environmental Surveyor","summary":"An Environmental Surveyor conducts field surveys and environmental assessments to collect reliable information about water, sediments, marine ecosystems, coastal areas, biodiversity, pollution, and environmental conditions. The role can support environmental impact assessments, marine construction, offshore energy, ports, coastal development, environmental monitoring, and regulatory compliance.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Marine Science / Oceanography"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a Marine Science / Oceanography graduate, a strong specialization is marine and coastal environmental surveying."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical route:"},{"type":"p","text":"B.Sc. Marine Science/Oceanography → Field/Environmental Internship → Environmental Surveyor / Environmental Field Technician → Senior Surveyor → Environmental Specialist / Project Lead → Environmental Consultant / Survey Manager"},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"Job titles and eligibility vary by employer. Some regulated environmental assessment, laboratory, diving, surveying, or safety activities may require additional qualifications or certifications."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons: 2026–2046","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2028"},{"text":"Student / Field Intern"},{"text":"Marine science + environmental sampling"}],[{"text":"2028–2030"},{"text":"Environmental Surveyor / Field Technician"},{"text":"Field surveys + environmental monitoring"}],[{"text":"2030–2033"},{"text":"Senior Environmental Surveyor"},{"text":"Independent surveys + data interpretation"}],[{"text":"2033–2037"},{"text":"Environmental Specialist"},{"text":"EIA, marine ecology, GIS, environmental compliance"}],[{"text":"2037–2042"},{"text":"Survey/Project Lead"},{"text":"Multi-disciplinary environmental projects"}],[{"text":"2042–2046"},{"text":"Environmental Consultant / Manager"},{"text":"Large projects + environmental strategy"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Key Skills","Proof"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Marine/environmental foundation"},{"text":"Oceanography, ecology, chemistry, geology"},{"text":"Field notes + basic project"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Survey science"},{"text":"Water/sediment sampling, biodiversity, pollution"},{"text":"Fieldwork + laboratory project"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Professional surveying"},{"text":"GIS, remote sensing, environmental monitoring"},{"text":"Survey project + internship"}],[{"text":"Year 4 (if applicable)"},{"text":"Industry readiness"},{"text":"EIA, reporting, statistics, marine survey technology"},{"text":"Industry internship + final project"}],[{"text":"Post-graduation"},{"text":"Specialization"},{"text":"Marine ecology, coastal monitoring, EIA, GIS or offshore surveys"},{"text":"Professional experience"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Build the Scientific Foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Physical oceanography"},{"text":"Chemical oceanography"},{"text":"Biological oceanography"},{"text":"Marine ecology"},{"text":"Marine geology"},{"text":"Environmental science"},{"text":"Chemistry"},{"text":"Physics"},{"text":"Mathematics"},{"text":"Statistics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Understand marine systems"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Waves"},{"text":"Tides"},{"text":"Currents"},{"text":"Salinity"},{"text":"Temperature"},{"text":"Dissolved oxygen"},{"text":"Nutrient cycles"},{"text":"Sediment transport"},{"text":"Coastal processes"},{"text":"Marine food webs"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Learn Environmental Surveying"},{"type":"p